IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `tad-dates`

-- Anti-Discrimination Act 1998 (Tas) -- the rules a person bringing a discrimination or prohibited-conduct complaint
-- meets: the prescribed attributes and the meaning of discrimination (Part 4 Division 1, ss 14-16), the prohibited
-- conduct (Part 4 Division 2, ss 17-21), the areas of activity (Division 3, s 22), the exceptions a respondent may prove
-- (Part 5 Divisions 1-10, ss 23-55, with s 101) and an exemption granted under Division 11 (as a fact, with the review
-- period of s 59), the complaint machinery as it meets the complainant (Part 6: ss 60, 60A, 62, 63, 64, 65, 66, 68(6),
-- (7), 71(4), (5), 72, 73, 78(2), 78(4), 80(4), 89, 90, 91, 92, 93, 99(3), 100(2)), and Part 7 as it meets the
-- complainant (ss 102, 104, 108).
--
-- This module holds the law. The questions are asked in tad-seat.l4, which IMPORTs it and never restates a rule.
-- Nothing here is exported.
--
-- ANSWERS. A yes/no rule answers JUST TRUE; JUST FALSE where the Act's own words say no ("means", "takes place if",
-- "does not apply", "only applies if", "may not ... without", "is not entitled", an "if" condition that fails); or
-- NOTHING where the Act does not answer on the facts given, with a "NOTHING-kind" comment. In particular a grant or
-- prohibition limited by its own wording (the ground, the setting, the conduct it names) answers NOTHING outside those
-- words, and JUST FALSE when its own "if" condition fails. Judgments the Act hands to someone else ("reasonable",
-- "reasonably necessary", "unjustifiable hardship", "genuine occupational qualification", "satisfied", "in the opinion
-- of the Commissioner", "in good faith") are inputs: the answer is conditional on them.
--
-- UNOFFICIAL. Based on material from the Tasmanian Legislation website (State of Tasmania, CC BY 4.0); not the
-- authorised version. See SOURCE-LICENSE.md. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `Anti-Discrimination Act 1998`

§§ `Helpers`

-- JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE, for the many "if" conditions.
GIVEN b IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`yes or no` b MEANS
    IF b
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE JUST FALSE

-- A grant or prohibition limited by its own wording and then by an "if": NOTHING outside its wording (NOTHING-kind:
-- limited by its own wording), then JUST TRUE or JUST FALSE on the condition.
GIVEN `within its wording` IS A BOOLEAN, `its condition` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`within` `within its wording` `then if` `its condition` MEANS
    IF NOT `within its wording`
    THEN NOTHING
    ELSE `yes or no` `its condition`

-- A grant or prohibition limited only by its own wording: JUST TRUE inside it, NOTHING outside (NOTHING-kind: limited
-- by its own wording).
GIVEN `within its wording` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`only within` `within its wording` MEANS
    IF `within its wording`
    THEN JUST TRUE
    ELSE NOTHING

§§ `s 16 -- the prescribed attributes`

-- s 16: "A person must not discriminate against another person on the ground of any of the following attributes".
-- s 3: "prescribed attribute means an attribute specified in section 16". The s 3 definitions (race, disability,
-- family responsibilities, irrelevant criminal record, gender identity and the rest) are glossed in the seat; whether
-- the person has an attribute, had it or is believed to have it is asked.
DECLARE `Attribute` IS ONE OF
    `race`
    `age`
    `sexual orientation`
    `lawful sexual activity`
    `gender`
    `gender identity`
    `sex characteristics`
    `marital status`
    `relationship status`
    `pregnancy`
    `breastfeeding`
    `parental status`
    `family responsibilities`
    `disability`
    `industrial activity`
    `political belief or affiliation`
    `political activity`
    `religious belief or affiliation`
    `religious activity`
    `irrelevant criminal record`
    `irrelevant medical record`
    `association with a person who has, or is believed to have, any of these attributes`
    `something else not listed`

-- "prescribed attribute means an attribute specified in section 16": a closed definition, so JUST FALSE otherwise.
GIVEN a IS AN `Attribute`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 16 -- it is a prescribed attribute` a MEANS
    `yes or no` (NOT (a EQUALS `something else not listed`))

-- The attributes s 17(1) names: "section 16(e), (a), (b), (c), (d), (ea), (eb) and (k), (f), (fa), (g), (h), (i) or (j)".
GIVEN a IS AN `Attribute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 17(1) names` a IF
    elem a (LIST `gender`, `race`, `age`, `sexual orientation`, `lawful sexual activity`, `gender identity`, `sex characteristics`, `disability`, `marital status`, `relationship status`, `pregnancy`, `breastfeeding`, `parental status`, `family responsibilities`)

-- The grounds s 19 names: race; disability; sexual orientation or lawful sexual activity; religious belief or
-- affiliation or religious activity; gender identity or sex characteristics.
GIVEN a IS AN `Attribute`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 19 names` a IF
    elem a (LIST `race`, `disability`, `sexual orientation`, `lawful sexual activity`, `religious belief or affiliation`, `religious activity`, `gender identity`, `sex characteristics`)

§§ `s 22 -- the areas of activity`

DECLARE `Area` IS ONE OF
    `employment`
    `education and training`
    `provision of facilities, goods and services`
    `accommodation`
    `membership and activities of clubs`
    `administration of any law of the State or any State program`
    `awards, enterprise agreements or industrial agreements`
    `none of these areas`

-- s 22(1): "this Act applies to discrimination and prohibited conduct, other than inciting hatred, by or against a person
-- engaged in, or undertaking any, activity in connection with any of the following". Outside the areas the Act states
-- its scope without "only": NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: scope limit without "only"; ruling of 2026-11-05 (c)).
GIVEN `the area` IS AN `Area`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `s 22 -- in an area` `the area` IF NOT (`the area` EQUALS `none of these areas`)

§§ `ss 14-16 -- discrimination`

-- s 14(2): "Direct discrimination takes place if a person treats another person on the basis of any prescribed
-- attribute, imputed prescribed attribute or a characteristic imputed to that attribute less favourably than a person
-- without that attribute or characteristic." s 14(3): it need not be the sole or dominant ground, and motive does not
-- matter. "takes place if": JUST FALSE when the treatment is not less favourable on that basis.
GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `the area` IS AN `Area`
      `treated less favourably on the basis of it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 14 -- direct discrimination` `the attribute` `the area` `treated less favourably on the basis of it` MEANS
    IF `the attribute` EQUALS `something else not listed`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `within` (`s 22 -- in an area` `the area`) `then if` `treated less favourably on the basis of it`

-- s 15(1): "Indirect discrimination takes place if a person imposes a condition, requirement or practice which is
-- unreasonable in the circumstances and has the effect of disadvantaging a member of a group of people who (a) share, or
-- are believed to share, a prescribed attribute; or (b) share ... any of the characteristics imputed to that attribute
-- more than a person who is not a member of that group." (2): awareness is not needed.
GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `the area` IS AN `Area`
      `imposed a condition, requirement or practice` IS A BOOLEAN
      `unreasonable in the circumstances` IS A BOOLEAN
      `disadvantages my group more` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 15 -- indirect discrimination` `the attribute` `the area` `imposed a condition, requirement or practice` `unreasonable in the circumstances` `disadvantages my group more` MEANS
    IF `the attribute` EQUALS `something else not listed`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `within` (`s 22 -- in an area` `the area`) `then if` (`imposed a condition, requirement or practice` AND `unreasonable in the circumstances` AND `disadvantages my group more`)

§§ `s 17 -- offensive conduct and sexual harassment`

-- s 17(1): "A person must not engage in any conduct which offends, humiliates, intimidates, insults or ridicules another
-- person on the basis of an attribute referred to in section 16(e), (a), (b), (c), (d), (ea), (eb) and (k), (f), (fa),
-- (g), (h), (i) or (j) in circumstances in which a reasonable person, having regard to all the circumstances, would have
-- anticipated that the other person would be offended, humiliated, intimidated, insulted or ridiculed." A prohibition
-- limited by its own wording: JUST TRUE inside it, NOTHING outside (fork F3). s 55 is asked separately.
GIVEN `the attribute` IS AN `Attribute`
      `the area` IS AN `Area`
      `the conduct offended, humiliated, intimidated, insulted or ridiculed me on that basis` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable person would have anticipated it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(1) -- offensive conduct` `the attribute` `the area` `the conduct offended, humiliated, intimidated, insulted or ridiculed me on that basis` `a reasonable person would have anticipated it` MEANS
    `only within` (`s 17(1) names` `the attribute` AND `s 22 -- in an area` `the area` AND `the conduct offended, humiliated, intimidated, insulted or ridiculed me on that basis` AND `a reasonable person would have anticipated it`)

DECLARE `Sexual conduct` IS ONE OF
    `physical contact of a sexual nature (s 17(3)(a))`
    `a sexual advance or a request for sexual favours (s 17(3)(b))`
    `a remark or statement with sexual connotations, to me or about me in my presence (s 17(3)(c))`
    `a gesture, action or comment of a sexual nature (s 17(3)(d))`
    `other conduct of a sexual nature in relation to me (s 17(3)(e))`
    `none of these`

-- s 17(2): "A person must not sexually harass another person." (3): "Sexual harassment takes place if a person" does one
-- of (a)-(e) -- (a) "unsolicited", (b)-(d) "unwelcome", (e) "offensive to that person" -- "in circumstances in which a
-- reasonable person ... would have anticipated that the other person would be offended, humiliated, intimidated,
-- insulted or ridiculed." "takes place if": JUST FALSE when it fails. s 22(1) confines prohibited conduct other than
-- inciting hatred to the areas: NOTHING outside them.
GIVEN `what they did` IS A `Sexual conduct`
      `the area` IS AN `Area`
      `it was unsolicited, unwelcome or offensive to me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a reasonable person would have anticipated it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 17(2), (3) -- sexual harassment` `what they did` `the area` `it was unsolicited, unwelcome or offensive to me` `a reasonable person would have anticipated it` MEANS
    IF `what they did` EQUALS `none of these`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `within` (`s 22 -- in an area` `the area`) `then if` (`it was unsolicited, unwelcome or offensive to me` AND `a reasonable person would have anticipated it`)

§§ `s 18 -- victimisation`

DECLARE `Reason for the detriment` IS ONE OF
    `I made, or intend to make, a complaint under the Act`
    `I gave, or intend to give, evidence or information in proceedings under the Act`
    `I alleged, or intend to allege, a contravention of the Act`
    `I refused, or intend to refuse, to do something that would contravene the Act`
    `I did something else under or by reference to the Act`
    `another reason`

-- s 18(1): "A person must not victimise another person because that other person" (a)-(e). (2): "Victimisation takes
-- place if a person subjects, or threatens to subject, another person or an associate of that other person to any
-- detriment." s 3: "detriment includes humiliation or denigration". No detriment: JUST FALSE ("takes place if"). A
-- detriment for another reason: NOTHING (the "because" limits the prohibition; fork F4). Outside the areas: NOTHING.
GIVEN `a detriment to me or my associate` IS A BOOLEAN
      `why they did it` IS A `Reason for the detriment`
      `the area` IS AN `Area`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 18 -- victimisation` `a detriment to me or my associate` `why they did it` `the area` MEANS
    IF NOT `a detriment to me or my associate`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `only within` ((NOT (`why they did it` EQUALS `another reason`)) AND `s 22 -- in an area` `the area`)

§§ `s 19 -- inciting hatred`

-- s 19: "A person, by a public act, must not incite hatred towards, serious contempt for, or severe ridicule of, a person
-- or a group of persons on the ground of" (a)-(e). s 22(2): it applies in any area. s 3: "public act includes" any
-- communication to the public, conduct observable by the public, or dissemination to the public (asked as a fact). A
-- prohibition limited by its own wording: JUST TRUE inside it, NOTHING outside. s 55 is asked separately.
GIVEN `the ground` IS AN `Attribute`
      `by a public act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it incited hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 19 -- inciting hatred` `the ground` `by a public act` `it incited hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule` MEANS
    `only within` (`s 19 names` `the ground` AND `by a public act` AND `it incited hatred, serious contempt or severe ridicule`)

§§ `s 20 -- signs, notices and advertisements`

-- s 20(1): "A person must not publish or display, or cause or permit to be published or displayed, any sign, notice or
-- advertising matter that promotes, expresses or depicts discrimination or prohibited conduct." (2): "Subsection (1)
-- does not apply to anything that is used for the purpose of discouraging discrimination or prohibited conduct." s 3:
-- "publish includes to authorise publication".
GIVEN `they published or displayed it` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it promotes, expresses or depicts discrimination or prohibited conduct` IS A BOOLEAN
      `used to discourage discrimination` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the area` IS AN `Area`
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 20 -- the sign or advertisement was prohibited` `they published or displayed it` `it promotes, expresses or depicts discrimination or prohibited conduct` `used to discourage discrimination` `the area` MEANS
    IF `used to discourage discrimination`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE `only within` (`they published or displayed it` AND `it promotes, expresses or depicts discrimination or prohibited conduct` AND `s 22 -- in an area` `the area`)

§§ `ss 21, 104 -- who else is liable`

-- s 21(1): "A person must not knowingly (a) cause ... (b) induce ... (c) aid another person to contravene this Act."
-- (2): "All persons referred to in subsection (1) are jointly and severally liable for any contravention under this
-- Act." Outside its wording (not knowingly, or no contravention): NOTHING.
GIVEN `someone contravened the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `another knowingly caused, induced or aided it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 21 -- the helper is jointly liable` `someone contravened the Act` `another knowingly caused, induced or aided it` MEANS
    `only within` (`someone contravened the Act` AND `another knowingly caused, induced or aided it`)

-- s 104(1): "An organisation is to ensure that ... (c) no member, officer, employee or agent of the organisation engages
-- in, repeats or continues such conduct." (2): it "is to take reasonable steps to ensure" the same. (3): "An organisation
-- that does not comply with this section is liable for any contravention of this Act committed by any of its members,
-- officers, employees and agents." Read literally, a contravention by one of its people is itself a failure of (1)(c),
-- so the organisation is liable (fork F6; finding 4). s 3: "organisation includes a council, a Government department ...
-- or a State authority"; whether the body is an organisation is asked.
GIVEN `the body is an organisation` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the person was its member, officer, employee or agent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `that person contravened the Act` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 104 -- the organisation is liable` `the body is an organisation` `the person was its member, officer, employee or agent` `that person contravened the Act` MEANS
    `only within` (`the body is an organisation` AND `the person was its member, officer, employee or agent` AND `that person contravened the Act`)

§§ `Part 5 -- the exceptions a respondent may prove (s 101)`

-- s 101: "A person who relies on an exception referred to in Part 5 as a defence to a complaint is to prove that
-- exception on the balance of probabilities." Each exception is limited by its own wording -- the ground (the attribute)
-- and the setting it names -- and most then by an "if". Outside the ground or the setting: NOTHING; when the "if"
-- fails: JUST FALSE. An exemption granted by the Commissioner (Division 11) is asked as a fact.
DECLARE `Exception` IS ONE OF
    `s 23: a charitable provision for persons with an attribute`
    `s 24: reasonably necessary to comply with a law or an order`
    `s 25: a scheme for a disadvantaged group or a group with a special need`
    `s 26: an equal opportunity program, plan or arrangement`
    `s 27(1)(a): gender, in a religious institution, required by its doctrines`
    `s 27(1)(b): gender, in education, for enrolment in one-gender schools or hostels`
    `s 27(1)(c): gender, in employment, for the residential care of persons under 18`
    `s 27(1)(d): gender, in employment, a genuine occupational qualification or requirement`
    `s 27(1)(e): gender, in shared accommodation for fewer than 5 adults`
    `s 27(1)(f): gender, facilities reasonably required for one gender only`
    `s 27(2): gender, the use of a club benefit`
    `s 27(3): gender, membership of a one-gender club`
    `s 28: family, parental, pregnancy, breastfeeding, marital or relationship status, special services imposing unjustifiable hardship`
    `s 29: competitive sport restricted to one gender aged 12 or more`
    `s 30(1)(a): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, Commonwealth prescribed standards`
    `s 30(1)(b): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data`
    `s 31: age, competitive sport for a particular age group`
    `s 32: age, membership of a club for a particular age group`
    `s 33(1)(a): age, superannuation, Commonwealth prescribed standards`
    `s 33(1)(b): age, superannuation, actuarial or statistical data`
    `s 34: age, annuity, insurance, loans, credit or finance, actuarial or statistical data`
    `s 35: age, retirement or voluntary severance`
    `s 36: age, employment, a genuine occupational qualification or age-based wage rates`
    `s 37: age, educational programs for a particular age group`
    `s 38: age, benefits and concessions for a particular age group`
    `s 39: age, a child required to be accompanied by an adult`
    `s 40: race, a club benefit to preserve a minority culture or reduce disadvantage`
    `s 41: race, employment, a genuine occupational qualification`
    `s 42: race, places of cultural or religious significance`
    `s 43(a): disability, competitive sport, restricting participation`
    `s 43(b): disability, competitive sport, excluding a person not reasonably capable`
    `s 44: disability, annuity, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data`
    `s 45(a): disability, employment, inherent requirements or unjustifiable hardship`
    `s 45(b): disability, employment, authenticity or welfare services`
    `s 46: disability, special educational facilities`
    `s 47: disability, an infectious disease and public health`
    `s 48(a): disability, access to public places, unjustifiable hardship`
    `s 48(b): disability, goods and services, unjustifiable hardship`
    `s 49: industrial activity, employment, a genuine occupational qualification`
    `s 50: irrelevant criminal record, the education, training or care of children`
    `s 51(1): religion, employment, a genuine occupational qualification`
    `s 51(2): religion, employment in a religious educational institution`
    `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution`
    `s 51A(4): religion, admission as a student under a religious admission policy`
    `s 52(a)-(c): religion, priests and religious observance`
    `s 52(d): religion, another act in accordance with religious doctrine`
    `s 53: political belief or activity, employment as an adviser or political staff`
    `s 54: age or disability, legal incapacity`
    `an exemption granted by the Commissioner (ss 56, 57)`

-- The religious grounds of ss 51, 51A and 52.
`the religious grounds` MEANS LIST `religious belief or affiliation`, `religious activity`

-- The grounds each exception names. An empty list means any ground (ss 23-26, 29 and a granted exemption).
GIVEN e IS AN `Exception`
GIVETH A LIST OF `Attribute`
`the grounds of` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 23: a charitable provision for persons with an attribute` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `s 24: reasonably necessary to comply with a law or an order` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `s 25: a scheme for a disadvantaged group or a group with a special need` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `s 26: an equal opportunity program, plan or arrangement` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `s 29: competitive sport restricted to one gender aged 12 or more` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `an exemption granted by the Commissioner (ss 56, 57)` THEN EMPTY
    WHEN `s 27(1)(a): gender, in a religious institution, required by its doctrines` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(1)(b): gender, in education, for enrolment in one-gender schools or hostels` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(1)(c): gender, in employment, for the residential care of persons under 18` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(1)(d): gender, in employment, a genuine occupational qualification or requirement` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(1)(e): gender, in shared accommodation for fewer than 5 adults` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(1)(f): gender, facilities reasonably required for one gender only` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(2): gender, the use of a club benefit` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 27(3): gender, membership of a one-gender club` THEN LIST `gender`
    WHEN `s 28: family, parental, pregnancy, breastfeeding, marital or relationship status, special services imposing unjustifiable hardship` THEN LIST `family responsibilities`, `parental status`, `pregnancy`, `breastfeeding`, `marital status`, `relationship status`
    WHEN `s 30(1)(a): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, Commonwealth prescribed standards` THEN LIST `gender`, `marital status`, `relationship status`
    WHEN `s 30(1)(b): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` THEN LIST `gender`, `marital status`, `relationship status`
    WHEN `s 31: age, competitive sport for a particular age group` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 32: age, membership of a club for a particular age group` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 33(1)(a): age, superannuation, Commonwealth prescribed standards` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 33(1)(b): age, superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 34: age, annuity, insurance, loans, credit or finance, actuarial or statistical data` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 35: age, retirement or voluntary severance` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 36: age, employment, a genuine occupational qualification or age-based wage rates` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 37: age, educational programs for a particular age group` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 38: age, benefits and concessions for a particular age group` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 39: age, a child required to be accompanied by an adult` THEN LIST `age`
    WHEN `s 40: race, a club benefit to preserve a minority culture or reduce disadvantage` THEN LIST `race`
    WHEN `s 41: race, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` THEN LIST `race`
    WHEN `s 42: race, places of cultural or religious significance` THEN LIST `race`
    WHEN `s 49: industrial activity, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` THEN LIST `industrial activity`
    WHEN `s 50: irrelevant criminal record, the education, training or care of children` THEN LIST `irrelevant criminal record`
    WHEN `s 51(1): religion, employment, a genuine occupational qualification` THEN `the religious grounds`
    WHEN `s 51(2): religion, employment in a religious educational institution` THEN `the religious grounds`
    WHEN `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution` THEN `the religious grounds`
    WHEN `s 51A(4): religion, admission as a student under a religious admission policy` THEN `the religious grounds`
    WHEN `s 52(a)-(c): religion, priests and religious observance` THEN `the religious grounds`
    WHEN `s 52(d): religion, another act in accordance with religious doctrine` THEN `the religious grounds`
    WHEN `s 53: political belief or activity, employment as an adviser or political staff` THEN LIST `political belief or affiliation`, `political activity`
    WHEN `s 54: age or disability, legal incapacity` THEN LIST `age`, `disability`
    OTHERWISE LIST `disability`

-- How each exception's words work after the ground: only a setting (NOTHING outside it), or a setting and an "if"
-- (JUST FALSE when the "if" fails), or an "if" with a further condition.
DECLARE `Exception shape` IS ONE OF
    `a setting only`
    `a setting and an if`
    `a setting, an if and a further condition`

GIVEN e IS AN `Exception`
GIVETH AN `Exception shape`
`the shape of` e MEANS
    CONSIDER e
    WHEN `s 23: a charitable provision for persons with an attribute` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 26: an equal opportunity program, plan or arrangement` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 29: competitive sport restricted to one gender aged 12 or more` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 31: age, competitive sport for a particular age group` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 35: age, retirement or voluntary severance` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 37: age, educational programs for a particular age group` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 38: age, benefits and concessions for a particular age group` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 40: race, a club benefit to preserve a minority culture or reduce disadvantage` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 43(a): disability, competitive sport, restricting participation` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 46: disability, special educational facilities` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 52(a)-(c): religion, priests and religious observance` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 52(d): religion, another act in accordance with religious doctrine` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 53: political belief or activity, employment as an adviser or political staff` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `an exemption granted by the Commissioner (ss 56, 57)` THEN `a setting only`
    WHEN `s 27(2): gender, the use of a club benefit` THEN `a setting, an if and a further condition`
    WHEN `s 30(1)(a): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, Commonwealth prescribed standards` THEN `a setting, an if and a further condition`
    WHEN `s 30(1)(b): gender, marital or relationship status, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` THEN `a setting, an if and a further condition`
    WHEN `s 33(1)(b): age, superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` THEN `a setting, an if and a further condition`
    WHEN `s 34: age, annuity, insurance, loans, credit or finance, actuarial or statistical data` THEN `a setting, an if and a further condition`
    WHEN `s 44: disability, annuity, insurance or superannuation, actuarial or statistical data` THEN `a setting, an if and a further condition`
    OTHERWISE `a setting and an if`

GIVEN a IS AN `Attribute`, e IS AN `Exception`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the ground of` a `fits` e IF
    IF `the grounds of` e EQUALS EMPTY
    THEN TRUE
    ELSE elem a (`the grounds of` e)

-- The exception, on the facts. `the number` is the number of adults sharing (s 27(1)(e)) or the person's age (ss 29,
-- 39); `the further condition` is the second limb of s 27(2), the disclosure to the Tribunal under ss 30(2), 33(2),
-- 34(2), 44(2) ("only applies if": JUST FALSE when not made), or, for s 51A(1), that the person was not already enrolled
-- (s 51A(2): "does not apply to a person who is enrolled": JUST FALSE).
GIVEN e IS AN `Exception`
      a IS AN `Attribute`
      `in the setting` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the further condition` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the number` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`Part 5 -- the exception covers it` e a `in the setting` `the condition` `the further condition` `the number` MEANS
    BRANCH
        -- s 51A(3): "Subsection (1) does not permit discrimination on any grounds referred to in section 16 other than
        -- those specified in that subsection" -- a flat negative, JUST FALSE. (2): not for an enrolled student.
        IF e EQUALS `s 51A(1): religion, admission as a student to a religious educational institution` THEN
            IF NOT (`the ground of` a `fits` e)
            THEN JUST FALSE
            ELSE `within` `in the setting` `then if` `the further condition`
        IF NOT (`the ground of` a `fits` e) THEN NOTHING
        -- s 27(1)(e): "if it is shared accommodation for less than 5 adult persons".
        IF e EQUALS `s 27(1)(e): gender, in shared accommodation for fewer than 5 adults` THEN
            `within` `in the setting` `then if` (`the condition` AND `the number` LESS THAN 5)
        -- s 29: "restricting participation to persons of one gender of 12 years of age or more"; a person under 12 is
        -- outside its words.
        IF e EQUALS `s 29: competitive sport restricted to one gender aged 12 or more` THEN
            `only within` (`in the setting` AND `the number` AT LEAST 12)
        -- s 39: "may discriminate against a child" (s 3: under 18) "if" the risk condition holds.
        IF e EQUALS `s 39: age, a child required to be accompanied by an adult` THEN
            `within` (`in the setting` AND `the number` LESS THAN 18) `then if` `the condition`
        IF `the shape of` e EQUALS `a setting only` THEN `only within` `in the setting`
        IF `the shape of` e EQUALS `a setting and an if` THEN `within` `in the setting` `then if` `the condition`
        OTHERWISE `within` `in the setting` `then if` (`the condition` AND `the further condition`)

§§ `s 55 -- public purpose`

DECLARE `Conduct complained of` IS ONE OF
    `conduct that offended, humiliated, intimidated, insulted or ridiculed me (s 17(1))`
    `inciting hatred (s 19)`
    `other conduct`

-- s 55: "The provisions of section 17(1) and section 19 do not apply if the person's conduct is (a) a fair report of a
-- public act; or (b) a communication or dissemination of a matter that is subject to a defence of absolute privilege in
-- proceedings for defamation; or (c) a public act done in good faith for (i) academic, artistic, scientific or research
-- purposes; or (ii) any purpose in the public interest." "do not apply if": JUST FALSE when none holds; other conduct:
-- NOTHING (limited by its own wording).
GIVEN `the conduct` IS A `Conduct complained of`
      `a fair report of a public act` IS A BOOLEAN
      `subject to absolute privilege` IS A BOOLEAN
      `a public act in good faith for an academic, artistic, scientific, research or public interest purpose` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 55 -- the public purpose exception covers it` `the conduct` `a fair report of a public act` `subject to absolute privilege` `a public act in good faith for an academic, artistic, scientific, research or public interest purpose` MEANS
    `within` (NOT (`the conduct` EQUALS `other conduct`)) `then if` (`a fair report of a public act` OR `subject to absolute privilege` OR `a public act in good faith for an academic, artistic, scientific, research or public interest purpose`)

§§ `s 59 -- review of an exemption`

-- s 59(2)-(4): an application for review is to be in writing and "made within 28 days after" (2) "publication of the
-- notice under section 58(1)" (grant or renewal), (3) "receipt of the statement referred to in section 57(4)"
-- (refusal), (4) "the condition is imposed or varied". `the starting day` is that day.
GIVEN `the starting day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 59 -- the last day to apply for review of an exemption` `the starting day` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the starting day`

§§ `s 60, s 60A -- who may complain`

DECLARE `Who is complaining` IS ONE OF
    `the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(a))`
    `the person it was directed against, for a class of people it was also directed against (s 60(1)(b))`
    `a trade union, for one member it was directed against (s 60(1)(c)(i))`
    `a trade union, for a class of members it was directed against (s 60(1)(c)(ii))`
    `an organisation it was directed against (s 60(1)(d))`
    `an agent of one of these (s 60(1)(e))`
    `another person on behalf of the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(f))`
    `a litigation guardian appointed by the Commissioner (s 60A)`
    `someone else`

-- s 60(1): "Any of the following may complain to the Commissioner". (b), (c)(ii), (d): "if the Commissioner is satisfied
-- that a majority of those members are likely to consent". (4): "A person may not make a complaint on behalf of another
-- person without the approval of the Commissioner" (JUST FALSE without it; applied to (e) an agent, (c)(i) a union for
-- one member and (f), fork F15). (3): "The Commissioner may accept a complaint
-- from a child if the Commissioner is satisfied that the child has sufficient maturity" (JUST FALSE for a child without
-- it; fork F7). s 60A(2): a litigation guardian "may make a complaint". The list is not closed with "only": someone else,
-- NOTHING (NOTHING-kind: list not closed).
GIVEN `who` IS A `Who is complaining`
      `the age of the person complaining` IS A NUMBER
      `the Commissioner is satisfied a majority are likely to consent` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner approved the complaint on another's behalf` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the Commissioner is satisfied a child complainant is mature enough` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 60 -- the complaint may be made` `who` `the age of the person complaining` `the Commissioner is satisfied a majority are likely to consent` `the Commissioner approved the complaint on another's behalf` `the Commissioner is satisfied a child complainant is mature enough` MEANS
    BRANCH
        IF `who` EQUALS `someone else` THEN NOTHING
        IF `a child without leave` THEN JUST FALSE
        IF `who` EQUALS `another person on behalf of the person it was directed against (s 60(1)(f))` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner approved the complaint on another's behalf`
        IF `who` EQUALS `an agent of one of these (s 60(1)(e))` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner approved the complaint on another's behalf`
        IF `who` EQUALS `a trade union, for one member it was directed against (s 60(1)(c)(i))` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner approved the complaint on another's behalf`
        IF `who` EQUALS `the person it was directed against, for a class of people it was also directed against (s 60(1)(b))` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner is satisfied a majority are likely to consent`
        IF `who` EQUALS `a trade union, for a class of members it was directed against (s 60(1)(c)(ii))` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner is satisfied a majority are likely to consent`
        IF `who` EQUALS `an organisation it was directed against (s 60(1)(d))` THEN `yes or no` `the Commissioner is satisfied a majority are likely to consent`
        OTHERWISE JUST TRUE
    WHERE
        `a child without leave` MEANS
                `the age of the person complaining` LESS THAN 18
            AND (NOT `the Commissioner is satisfied a child complainant is mature enough`)
            AND (NOT (`who` EQUALS `a litigation guardian appointed by the Commissioner (s 60A)`))

§§ `ss 66, 68, 73, 108 -- bars to complaining`

DECLARE `Earlier step` IS ONE OF
    `nothing earlier`
    `I agreed with them not to complain (s 66)`
    `I withdrew a complaint about the same matter (s 68(6))`
    `I withdrew a complaint about the same matter, but not voluntarily (s 68(7))`
    `an earlier complaint about the same matter lapsed (ss 65(4), 71(5), 72(1))`

-- s 108(1): "This Act does not apply to discrimination or prohibited conduct that took place and concluded before the
-- commencement of this Act." s 66(1): the Commissioner "may accept a complaint from a person who had previously agreed
-- ... not to complain if the Commissioner reasonably believes that it is fair to do so". s 68(6): a complainant who
-- withdraws "is not entitled to make another complaint in relation to the same matter without the permission of the
-- Commissioner". s 68(7): the Commissioner "may allow a person who has withdrawn a complaint involuntarily to reinstitute
-- the complaint if the Commissioner considers it is in the public interest". s 73: a complainant whose complaint lapses
-- under s 65(4), 71(5) or 72(1) "is not entitled to make another complaint in relation to the same matter".
GIVEN `it all took place and ended before the Act commenced` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the earlier step` IS AN `Earlier step`
      `the Commissioner allows it` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 66, 68, 73, 108 -- nothing bars the complaint` `it all took place and ended before the Act commenced` `the earlier step` `the Commissioner allows it` MEANS
    IF `it all took place and ended before the Act commenced`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the earlier step`
         WHEN `nothing earlier` THEN JUST TRUE
         WHEN `an earlier complaint about the same matter lapsed (ss 65(4), 71(5), 72(1))` THEN JUST FALSE
         OTHERWISE `yes or no` `the Commissioner allows it`

§§ `s 62 -- the form of a complaint`

-- s 62(1): "A complaint is to (a) be made in writing and signed by the complainant; and (b) identify the person, class
-- of persons or organisation against whom the alleged discrimination or prohibited conduct was directed and against whom
-- the complaint is made; and (c) set out details ...; and (d) be lodged with the Commissioner (i) in person; or (ii) by
-- post; or (iii) by any other means the Commissioner allows." A bare "is to" not met: JUST FALSE (fork F8).
GIVEN `in writing and signed` IS A BOOLEAN
      `identifies who it was directed against and who it is against` IS A BOOLEAN
      `sets out the details` IS A BOOLEAN
      `lodged in person, by post or by a means the Commissioner allows` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 62 -- the complaint is in the required form` `in writing and signed` `identifies who it was directed against and who it is against` `sets out the details` `lodged in person, by post or by a means the Commissioner allows` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`in writing and signed` AND `identifies who it was directed against and who it is against` AND `sets out the details` AND `lodged in person, by post or by a means the Commissioner allows`)

§§ `Regulative rules for the complainant's steps`

-- The complainant's steps with a time limit are modelled as obligations: MUST take the step WITHIN the days allowed,
-- with the consequence the Act gives on failure. The helper runs a rule over the day of the step: a CONSIDER on an
-- EVALTRACE can match FULFILLED but not BREACH on the stable l4, so FULFILLED means in time and anything else late. It
-- takes a DEONTIC value, so it is never exported.
DECLARE `Party` IS ONE OF
    `the complainant`
    `the Commissioner`

DECLARE `Step` IS ONE OF
    `make the complaint`
    `accept the complaint out of time`
    `apply to the Tribunal for review`
    `appeal to the Supreme Court`

GIVEN `the rule` IS A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
      `the actor` IS A `Party`
      `the step` IS A `Step`
      `the time of the step` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
DECIDE `the step satisfies` `the rule` `by` `the actor` `doing` `the step` `at` `the time of the step` IF
    CONSIDER EVALTRACE `the rule` 0 (LIST (WAITUNTIL `the time of the step`), (EVENT `the actor` `the step` `the time of the step`))
    WHEN FULFILLED THEN TRUE
    OTHERWISE FALSE

§§ `s 63 -- the time limit for a complaint`

-- s 63(1): "A complaint is to be made within 12 months after the alleged discrimination or prohibited conduct took
-- place." (2): "The Commissioner may accept a complaint made after the 12-month time limitation has expired if satisfied
-- that it is reasonable to do so." The last day is the same day 12 months on (fork F1).
GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 63 -- the last day to complain` `the day of the conduct` MEANS `the date` 12 `months after` `the day of the conduct`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the complaint is to be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `make the complaint`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST
        PARTY `the Commissioner`
        MAY `accept the complaint out of time`

DECLARE `Complaint timing` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `late, but the Commissioner may accept it if satisfied that it is reasonable to do so (s 63(2))`
    `not answered: that day is before the conduct`

GIVEN `the day of the conduct` IS A DATE, `the day of complaining` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Complaint timing`
`s 63 -- the complaint is in time` `the day of the conduct` `the day of complaining` MEANS
    IF `the day of complaining` `is before` `the day of the conduct`
    THEN `not answered: that day is before the conduct`
    ELSE IF `the step satisfies` (`the complaint is to be made within` `the days allowed here`) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `make the complaint` `at` `the time of complaining`
         THEN `in time`
         ELSE `late, but the Commissioner may accept it if satisfied that it is reasonable to do so (s 63(2))`
    WHERE
        `the days allowed here` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the conduct` `to` (`s 63 -- the last day to complain` `the day of the conduct`)
        `the time of complaining` MEANS `the days from` `the day of the conduct` `to` `the day of complaining`

§§ `s 64 -- acceptance or rejection`

DECLARE `Rejection ground` IS ONE OF
    `trivial, vexatious, misconceived or lacking in substance, in the Commissioner's opinion (s 64(1)(a))`
    `not about discrimination or prohibited conduct (s 64(1)(b))`
    `I have started proceedings elsewhere on the same events, with similar remedies (s 64(1)(c))`
    `someone else has started proceedings on the same subject matter, and the Commissioner is satisfied it can be dealt with there (s 64(1)(d))`
    `a more appropriate remedy is reasonably available, in the Commissioner's opinion (s 64(1)(e))`
    `already adequately dealt with by the Commissioner or a State or Commonwealth authority (s 64(1)(f))`
    `better dealt with by a State or Commonwealth authority, in the Commissioner's opinion (s 64(1)(g))`
    `within an exemption granted under Division 11 of Part 5, in the Commissioner's opinion (s 64(1)(h))`
    `none of these`

-- s 64(1): "The Commissioner may reject any complaint if" (a)-(h). The opinion or satisfaction, and the facts, are one
-- input: whether the ground is made out. No ground: JUST FALSE ("may reject ... if").
GIVEN `the ground` IS A `Rejection ground`, `the ground is made out` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 64 -- the Commissioner may reject the complaint` `the ground` `the ground is made out` MEANS
    `yes or no` ((NOT (`the ground` EQUALS `none of these`)) AND `the ground is made out`)

-- s 64(2): "The Commissioner is to decide whether to accept or reject a complaint within 42 days after its receipt."
GIVEN `the day received` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 64 -- the last day for the decision` `the day received` MEANS `the date` 42 `days after` `the day received`

§§ `ss 65, 71, 72, 73 -- review by the Tribunal`

DECLARE `Commissioner decision` IS ONE OF
    `my complaint was rejected (s 64)`
    `my complaint was not accepted`
    `my complaint was dismissed after investigation (s 71)`

-- s 65(3): an application for review of a rejection or non-acceptance is to be "made within 28 days after receipt of
-- notification of the statement"; (4): if not, "the complaint lapses at the end of that period". s 71(4): for a
-- dismissal, "within 28 days after receipt of the statement"; (5): if not, "the complaint lapses". s 73: no further
-- complaint about the same matter.
GIVEN `the day I received the statement` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`ss 65, 71 -- the last day to apply for review` `the day I received the statement` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day I received the statement`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the review application is to be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `apply to the Tribunal for review`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "no application for review within 28 days: the complaint lapses, and no further complaint may be made about the same matter (ss 65(4), 71(5), 73)"

DECLARE `Review timing` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `too late: the complaint has lapsed, and you cannot complain again about the same matter (ss 65(4), 71(5), 73)`
    `not answered: that day is before the statement was received`

GIVEN `the day I received the statement` IS A DATE, `the day I apply` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Review timing`
`ss 65, 71 -- the review application is in time` `the day I received the statement` `the day I apply` MEANS
    IF `the day I apply` `is before` `the day I received the statement`
    THEN `not answered: that day is before the statement was received`
    ELSE IF `the step satisfies` (`the review application is to be made within` 28) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `apply to the Tribunal for review` `at` (`the days from` `the day I received the statement` `to` `the day I apply`)
         THEN `in time`
         ELSE `too late: the complaint has lapsed, and you cannot complain again about the same matter (ss 65(4), 71(5), 73)`

DECLARE `Review outcome` IS ONE OF
    `the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same matter (ss 72(1), 73)`
    `the complaint goes back to the Commissioner for investigation (s 72(2))`
    `the Tribunal deals with the complaint as an inquiry (s 72(3))`
    `the complaint goes back to the Commissioner to accept or reject it (s 72(4))`

-- s 72: if the Tribunal "is satisfied that the Commissioner made a correct decision ... the complaint lapses" (1); if
-- not, a rejection goes back for investigation (2), a dismissal is dealt with as an inquiry (3), a non-acceptance goes
-- back for acceptance or rejection (4).
GIVEN `the decision` IS A `Commissioner decision`, `the Tribunal is satisfied it was correct` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A `Review outcome`
`s 72 -- what the review leads to` `the decision` `the Tribunal is satisfied it was correct` MEANS
    IF `the Tribunal is satisfied it was correct`
    THEN `the complaint lapses, and you cannot complain again about the same matter (ss 72(1), 73)`
    ELSE CONSIDER `the decision`
         WHEN `my complaint was rejected (s 64)` THEN `the complaint goes back to the Commissioner for investigation (s 72(2))`
         WHEN `my complaint was dismissed after investigation (s 71)` THEN `the Tribunal deals with the complaint as an inquiry (s 72(3))`
         WHEN `my complaint was not accepted` THEN `the complaint goes back to the Commissioner to accept or reject it (s 72(4))`

§§ `ss 78, 100 -- referral to the Tribunal, and the appeal from a s 78(4) dismissal`

-- s 78(2): the Commissioner "is to refer a complaint to the Tribunal within 6 months after notification under section 67
-- or within any further period agreed with the complainant". `the day of notification` is the day the respondent was
-- notified of the acceptance under s 67.
GIVEN `the day of notification` IS A DATE
      `a further period was agreed with me` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the agreed last day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 78 -- the last day for referral` `the day of notification` `a further period was agreed with me` `the agreed last day` MEANS
    IF `a further period was agreed with me`
    THEN `the agreed last day`
    ELSE `the date` 6 `months after` `the day of notification`

-- s 78(4): the Commissioner "may decline to refer a complaint to the Tribunal and dismiss the complaint if the
-- complainant has, in the opinion of the Commissioner, failed to pursue the complaint". s 100(2): "A person may appeal to
-- the Supreme Court against a decision under section 78(4) within 28 days after the decision was made."
GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 100 -- the last day to appeal` `the day of the decision` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the decision`

GIVEN `the days allowed` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A DEONTIC `Party` `Step`
`the appeal is to be made within` `the days allowed` MEANS
    PARTY `the complainant`
    MUST `appeal to the Supreme Court`
    WITHIN `the days allowed`
    HENCE FULFILLED
    LEST BREACH BY `the complainant` BECAUSE "no appeal within 28 days after the s 78(4) decision (s 100(2))"

DECLARE `Appeal timing` IS ONE OF
    `in time`
    `too late: the 28 days in s 100(2) have passed`
    `not answered: that day is before the decision`

GIVEN `the day of the decision` IS A DATE, `the day I appeal` IS A DATE
GIVETH A `Appeal timing`
`s 100 -- the appeal is in time` `the day of the decision` `the day I appeal` MEANS
    IF `the day I appeal` `is before` `the day of the decision`
    THEN `not answered: that day is before the decision`
    ELSE IF `the step satisfies` (`the appeal is to be made within` 28) `by` `the complainant` `doing` `appeal to the Supreme Court` `at` (`the days from` `the day of the decision` `to` `the day I appeal`)
         THEN `in time`
         ELSE `too late: the 28 days in s 100(2) have passed`

§§ `s 80(4) -- the directions conference`

-- s 80(4): "The Tribunal, if the complainant does not, without reasonable excuse, comply with a requirement to attend a
-- directions conference in respect of that complaint, may (a) dismiss the complaint; and (b) order the complainant to
-- pay costs to the respondent." "if": JUST FALSE when the complainant attended or had a reasonable excuse.
GIVEN `I was required to attend` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I attended` IS A BOOLEAN
      `I had a reasonable excuse` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 80 -- the Tribunal may dismiss and order costs` `I was required to attend` `I attended` `I had a reasonable excuse` MEANS
    `yes or no` (`I was required to attend` AND (NOT `I attended`) AND (NOT `I had a reasonable excuse`))

§§ `ss 89, 91, 92, 99 -- what the Tribunal may order`

DECLARE `Order` IS ONE OF
    `not to repeat or continue the conduct (s 89(1)(a))`
    `redress my loss, injury or humiliation (s 89(1)(b))`
    `re-employ me (s 89(1)(c))`
    `pay me compensation within a specified period (s 89(1)(d))`
    `pay a fine of up to 20 penalty units (s 89(1)(e))`
    `vary a contract or agreement or declare it void (s 89(1)(f))`
    `no further action (s 89(1)(g))`
    `any other appropriate order (s 89(1)(h))`
    `the Minister to exercise State Service Act powers (s 89(2))`
    `an apology or retraction (s 92)`
    `referral of the award or agreement to the Industrial Commission (s 91)`

-- s 89(1): "If the Tribunal finds after an inquiry that a complaint is substantiated, it may make one or more of the
-- following orders". (2): against "a State Service officer or State Service employee". s 91(1): a complaint "relating to
-- an award, enterprise agreement or industrial agreement" substantiated: the Tribunal "is to refer". s 92(1): "In respect
-- of a substantiated complaint, the Tribunal may require the respondent to (a) apologise ... (b) make any retractions".
-- Each "if": JUST FALSE when it fails.
GIVEN `the order` IS AN `Order`
      `substantiated after an inquiry` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the respondent is a State Service officer or employee` IS A BOOLEAN
      `it relates to an award or agreement` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`ss 89, 91, 92 -- the Tribunal may make the order` `the order` `substantiated after an inquiry` `the respondent is a State Service officer or employee` `it relates to an award or agreement` MEANS
    IF NOT `substantiated after an inquiry`
    THEN JUST FALSE
    ELSE CONSIDER `the order`
         WHEN `the Minister to exercise State Service Act powers (s 89(2))` THEN `yes or no` `the respondent is a State Service officer or employee`
         WHEN `referral of the award or agreement to the Industrial Commission (s 91)` THEN `yes or no` `it relates to an award or agreement`
         OTHERWISE JUST TRUE

-- s 89(1)(e): "a specified fine not exceeding 20 penalty units". The value of a penalty unit is set under other law, not
-- deposited: the answer is in penalty units.
`s 89 -- the largest fine on the respondent in penalty units` MEANS 20

-- s 99(3): "If the Tribunal dismisses a complaint on the ground that it is vexatious, it may order the complainant to pay
-- a specified fine not exceeding 10 penalty units." Otherwise s 99(3) gives no fine: 0.
GIVEN `dismissed as vexatious` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A NUMBER
`s 99 -- the largest fine on the complainant in penalty units` `dismissed as vexatious` MEANS
    IF `dismissed as vexatious`
    THEN 10
    ELSE 0

§§ `s 93 -- reasons for an order`

-- s 93: the Tribunal, "if requested by a complainant or respondent, is to give reasons in writing for an order made under
-- section 89". (2): the request is to be in writing and "made within 28 days after the date of the determination".
GIVEN `the day of the determination` IS A DATE
GIVETH A DATE
`s 93 -- the last day to ask for reasons` `the day of the determination` MEANS `the date` 28 `days after` `the day of the determination`

§§ `ss 76, 90, 94 -- enforcing an order or agreement`

DECLARE `What to enforce` IS ONE OF
    `an order of the Tribunal under s 89(1)`
    `an agreement recorded by the Commissioner (s 76)`
    `an agreement recorded by the Tribunal (s 94)`
    `another order`

-- s 90(1): a person "may enforce an order made under section 89(1) or an agreement to resolve a complaint by filing ...
-- free of charge, in the Supreme Court" a certified copy of the order (a) or of the s 76 record (b), and "(c) an
-- affidavit stating the extent to which the order or agreement has not been complied with." (2): "If the documents are
-- filed in accordance with this section, the order ... or agreement is enforceable as if it were an order of the Supreme
-- Court." "If": JUST FALSE until filed. Another order: NOTHING (s 90 names only s 89(1) orders and agreements).
GIVEN `what` IS A `What to enforce`, `I filed the certified copy and the affidavit` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 90 -- enforceable as a Supreme Court order` `what` `I filed the certified copy and the affidavit` MEANS
    `within` (NOT (`what` EQUALS `another order`)) `then if` `I filed the certified copy and the affidavit`

§§ `s 102 -- immunity for complainants and witnesses`

-- s 102: "A person is not liable to any action, claim or demand in respect of any loss, damage or injury suffered by
-- another person by reason only that the person in good faith (a) lodged a complaint with the Commissioner; or (b)
-- provided information or evidence to the Commissioner or Tribunal." Limited by its own words: NOTHING outside them.
GIVEN `I lodged a complaint or gave information or evidence` IS A BOOLEAN
      `in good faith` IS A BOOLEAN
      `the claim is only because of that` IS A BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
`s 102 -- I am immune` `I lodged a complaint or gave information or evidence` `in good faith` `the claim is only because of that` MEANS
    `only within` (`I lodged a complaint or gave information or evidence` AND `in good faith` AND `the claim is only because of that`)
